# kin/child/legs/std: the child's legs, short trousers over chunky boots (21 px body; regions: T thigh, K knee, S shin, B boot, O sole)
# THE SIDE WALK, the motion rebuild (2026-10-21; docs/MOTION_P2.md 5.5, STYLE_P2 10 "The owner's motion reference"): each
# side (R, L) walk key is two continuous limbs at the child's scale, hip (F-5 seat) > the trouser knee row (F-4) > the
# shin (the boot's top row F-3) > the foot, one boot in five hand-drawn tilts (maps/stamps/boots_child.stamps: C0 flat,
# C1 toe-up, C2 heel-up, C3 toe-off, C4 pointed; near and far; R and L re-lit), placed by `put`. Walk (cycle 12; plants =
# the planted heel 1:-1, -1:-3, -3:-5): contact walkA / walkC, the front C1 landing on its heel at +1, toe up two rows, the
# back C2 up on its toe pad at -2 (motion fix round 3: two px of daylight between the boots on F-2, so neither reads as
# a notch in the other; the down frame's C3 at -3 is the 1 px registration tolerance), the heel two rows up beside the
# back knee; down walkA2 / walkC2, the front C0 planted at -1, the back C3 rolled onto its toe at -3; pass walkB2 / walkD2
# (the child's own bob -1; fix round 3), the planted C0 at -3 straight under the hips (a 4 px column), the swing knee
# driven forward out of the tunic (these two keys draw on the hangFront layer, so the knee row F-6 shows over the hem's
# front half: the knee lifting the hem), a 3 px shin under it and the C3 toe down AHEAD of the planted toe (toe +6, lifted
# 2): the two boots apart by daylight (BOOTSPLIT), the swing foot hanging from a knee, not out from under the hem. Walk
# keys mark no stretch row (stretch 0). The left views: the right views mirrored and re-lit, the seat trimmed under the
# hem.
# History (superseded for the side walk and run by the rebuild above; front and back keys, the idles and the other
# keys are unchanged):
# kin/child/legs/std: the child's legs (KIN-CHILD, P2b wave 2; first drawn in the slice by FOLK-BODY): short trousers over
# chunky boots (each boot 5 px, 6 at the toe), 21 px body (STYLE_P2 3). Regions: T thigh (the hip row), K knee (the one
# trouser row that shows), B boot, O sole: rags bare the feet, kilts bare the knee. The walk keeps the idle's leg mass:
# boots never rotated (the idle boot moved and lifted a row), the planted leg straight under the hips; front and back
# walk in place (walkA: the screen-left foot lifted, walkC: the screen-right); side views 6 drawings over a 12 px cycle
# (the planted foot steps 2 / 2 / 2 px). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
use person
body child
role legs std
layer legs
anchor pivot
keys legs
stamps boots_child
tags boots-stamped

